Nexus-BS: asynchronous engine watchdog and a configurable high-speed bulk NAK reload.

- usbh_ehci_async_watchdog() (polled by the glue's interrupt thread, critical section held):
  a QH on the ring whose overlay is inactive while its next qTD is active, or a doorbell left
  unanswered, for CONFIG_USB_EHCI_ASYNC_KICK_US restarts the asynchronous schedule: ASE off,
  wait for ASS clear (EHCI 4.8), hand back the QHs of the running cycle, the waiting and the
  quarantined ones (the controller is not traversing and holds none, EHCI 4.8.2), point
  ASYNCLISTADDR at the head, ASE on, wait for ASS. The ChipIdea core parks on a stale QH
  copy (board build 84, libbsd stack before); the stock usbh_kill_urb() PSE/ASE toggle that
  patches/0004 removed used to get it out of that by accident.
- CONFIG_USB_EHCI_BULK_RL_HS: NAK reload of high-speed bulk QHs (default EHCI_TUNE_RL_HS).

diff --git a/port/ehci/usb_hc_ehci.c b/port/ehci/usb_hc_ehci.c
index 2f12280..d0266ee 100644
--- a/port/ehci/usb_hc_ehci.c
+++ b/port/ehci/usb_hc_ehci.c
@@ -58,6 +58,17 @@ volatile uint32_t g_ehci_xacterr_retries;
 #ifndef CONFIG_USB_EHCI_IAA_SPIN_US
 #define CONFIG_USB_EHCI_IAA_SPIN_US 500 /* usbh_kill_urb(): poll, then sleep 1 ms per check */
 #endif
